Scheme ID	"SCH001"
Scheme Name	"Coffee Development"
Category	"Agriculture, Rural & Environment"
Description	"A scheme related to the development of the coffee sector."
Benefits	"50% subsidy on the unit cost of coffee expansion (₹1,12,500 per hectare, based on the 2024–25 to 2025–26 guidelines). Paid in two instalments: 60% and 40%."
Eligibility	"ST, SC and other eligible growers; land must be suitable for coffee cultivation. Land records must be in the applicant's name. Seeds/seedlings must be obtained from the Coffee Board or approved nodal agency."
Application Process	"Submit the application and required documents to the concerned Coffee Board Extension Office after planting. Officials verify documents and inspect the field before recommending subsidy."
Documents Required	"Application form, self-declaration, Aadhaar or other valid photo ID, land ownership proof, and bank account details (account number, bank name, branch and IFSC)."
FAQs	"No FAQs available in the information I could verify. Check the official myScheme page for updates."
