Scheme ID	"SCH003"
Scheme Name	"National Means-cum-Merit Scholarship Scheme (NMMSS)"
Category	"Education & Scholarships"
Description	"Government scholarship scheme that supports meritorious students from economically weaker families to continue education after Class 8."
Benefits	"₹12,000 per year, paid directly into the selected student's bank account."
Eligibility	"Students entering Class 9 in government, government-aided or local body schools; parental income must not exceed ₹3.5 lakh per year. Minimum 55% in Class 7 to appear for the selection test (50% for SC/ST). Must qualify in the state selection test."
Application Process	"Complete One-Time Registration (OTR) on the National Scholarship Portal (NSP), apply online, and complete institute and district-level verification."
Documents Required	"Class 7 marksheet, parental income certificate, bank account details and other documents requested during NSP verification."
FAQs	"1. Who can apply? Eligible Class 9 students. 2. What is the scholarship amount? ₹12,000 yearly. 3. Is there a selection test? Yes, conducted by the State/UT. 4. Can it continue after Class 9? Yes, through renewal up to Class 12, subject to conditions."
Official Source URL	"https://scholarships.gov.in/"
official_url	"https://scholarships.gov.in/"
