Scheme ID	"SCH005"
Scheme Name	"Pradhan Mantri Matru Vandana Yojana (PMMVY)"
Category	"Women & Child Development"
Description	"Maternity benefit scheme providing financial assistance to eligible pregnant and lactating women."
Benefits	"₹5,000 for the first child in two instalments. ₹6,000 for the second child if the child is a girl, in one instalment."
Eligibility	"Eligible pregnant and lactating women aged 18 years 7 months to 55 years at childbirth who meet at least one specified social or economic eligibility category, such as SC/ST, BPL, e-Shram, MGNREGA or family income below ₹8 lakh annually."
Application Process	"Apply through the official PMMVY portal using citizen registration, or get assistance from an Anganwadi worker or ASHA worker. Complete the required pregnancy registration, health check-ups and verification."
Documents Required	"Aadhaar card, Aadhaar-linked bank/post office account details, MCP/RCHI card, mobile number and proof of eligibility. Childbirth and immunisation details are required for later instalments."
FAQs	"1. What is the benefit for the first child? ₹5,000. 2. What about the second child? ₹6,000 if the child is a girl. 3. Is Aadhaar required? Yes. 4. Where can women apply? Online or through an Anganwadi/ASHA worker."
Official Source URL	"https://wcd.gov.in/women/pradhan-mantri-matru-vandana-yojna"
official_url	"https://wcd.gov.in/women/pradhan-mantri-matru-vandana-yojna"
