Scheme ID	"SCH012"
Scheme Name	"Atal Pension Yojana (APY)"
Category	"Pension & Social Security"
Description	"Government-backed pension scheme that helps people save regularly during their working years and receive a guaranteed minimum monthly pension after retirement."
Benefits	"Guaranteed monthly pension of ₹1,000, ₹2,000, ₹3,000, ₹4,000 or ₹5,000 after reaching 60 years of age, depending on the pension option and contributions."
Eligibility	"Indian citizens aged 18–40 years with a savings bank or post office savings account. Anyone who is or has been an income-tax payer is not eligible to open a new APY account from 1 October 2022."
Application Process	"Visit the bank or post office where the savings account is held. Fill out the APY registration form and provide the required details. Contributions are automatically debited from the account."
Documents Required	"Savings bank account details, Aadhaar details (if provided), mobile number, nominee details and spouse details, where applicable."
FAQs	"FAQs: Who can apply? Indian citizens aged 18–40 who meet the conditions. When does pension start? At age 60. What is the monthly pension? ₹1,000 to ₹5,000. Is it free? No, regular contributions are required."
