Application Process	"Visit the official PMFME portal, register and submit the online application with the required project details. Applicants can also seek assistance from a District Resource Person (DRP) for preparing the project report and completing the application."
Documents Required	"Aadhaar or identity proof, address proof, bank account details, business information, project report, machinery quotations and other documents required by the lending bank and implementing department."
FAQs	"Q1. What is the subsidy? 35% of eligible project cost, up to ₹10 lakh for an individual unit. Q2. Can new businesses apply? The scheme provides support for eligible new and existing units. Q3. Can SHGs benefit? Yes. Q4. Does it provide training? Yes, entrepreneurship and food-processing training are included."
Official Source URL	"https://www.mofpi.gov.in/schemes/pmfme"
